; Draw-queue job template for a masked sprite
;
; The 16-byte record that #R$9836 fills in and #R$98B1 copies to the end of the draw queue at $C000 (the copy also takes
; the 5 bytes of code after the template, which are not used). #R$97B7 runs the queue: it calls the handler in the first
; word with DE = job address + 1 and clears the word. The handler #R$9972 consumes the fields as it draws. Fields:
; .
; +0 word: handler address (#R$9972)
; +2 word: address of the graphics in the sprite sheet, clipped (D = pixel row, E = column)
; +4 byte: character rows covered
; +5 byte: first character row (0-21)
; +6 byte: character column (0-31)
; +7 byte: offset of the first pixel row inside its character row, in 2-pixel units (0-3); cleared once used
; +8 byte: height still to draw, in 2-pixel units
; +9 byte: width in bytes (1-5)
; +10 byte: attribute of the cells
@label=SpriteJob
g$98D9 DEFW $9972    ; +0: handler
@label=SpriteJobGfx
 $98DB DEFW $0000    ; +2: graphics address
@label=SpriteJobRows
 $98DD DEFB $00      ; +4: character rows covered
@label=SpriteJobCell
 $98DE DEFW $0000    ; +5: row (low byte), +6: column (high byte)
@label=SpriteJobSubRow
 $98E0 DEFB $00      ; +7: first row offset
@label=SpriteJobHeight
 $98E1 DEFB $00      ; +8: height
@label=SpriteJobWidth
 $98E2 DEFB $00      ; +9: width
@label=SpriteJobAttr
 $98E3 DEFB $00      ; +10: attribute
